Z||000000||Heisenhund||06-13-2001||10:29 AM||||Hi all,<P>Newest dilemma:<BR>After completing the clutch replacemnent outlined on The Fiero Factory website (not nearly as painful as dropping the cradle!), I now have a "shimmy" when under moderate to heavy acceleration at about 20 through 35 MPH. It feels as if my Fiero is trying to attract a mate by wiggling its rear. The <BR>movement doesn't send the car out of control, but it was quite disconcerting when it first appeared as a problem.<P>Initial attempts at repair:<BR>Had wheels & tires revbalanced, replaced front transaxle mount that had broken during the operation, replaced strut nut (one of the 3 on top of the strut) that had stripped out during the reassembly, replaced dogbone as the old one was on its last legs, relubed everything (not really due for another 2000 <BR>miles, but I figured what the hell).<P>Results:<BR>Shimmy is not nearly as bad, but still present & quite noticable. My wife is afraid to ride in the car now. Not always a bad thing, but there are occasions where her company is desired (or required).<P>I'm open to ideas, suggestions and past experiences of this nature.<P>Thanks,<BR>Heis<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||06-13-2001||01:31 PM||||my suggestion would be to get your rear wheels aligned.I replaced my clutch about a year ago and after I was done I took the car out for test drive and every time I hit a small bump the car would jump around .I went and had it the rear wheels aligned and the problem went away.so your cars rear wheels are probobly out of alignement.good luck||||reg||1
